# Web Platform Architecture

Read `00-brand-core.mdc` first. Commercial positioning for public copy comes from
`THP-SMB-SERVICE-001` (`the-hard-port-os/knowledge/smb-service/THP-SMB-SERVICE-001-offer-architecture.md`).

## Stack (decided — do not re-litigate without explicit human request)

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Web | **Next.js 15** App Router (`apps/web/app/`) |
| API | **NestJS** + Prisma + Postgres (`apps/api/`) |
| Deploy | Docker Compose / Dokploy; web uses Next `output: 'standalone'` |

TanStack Start is retired. Do not add TanStack Router/Start dependencies back to `apps/web`.

## Route map

| Route | Audience | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Public applicants | None |
| `/work-with-us` | Public — full service explanation | None |
| `/apply` | Public — Engagement Readiness Application | None |
| `/about` | Public | None |
| `/sign-in` | THP operators/reviewers only | OAuth entry |
| `/review` | THP operators — application list | JWT (client-side) |
| `/auth/callback` | OAuth handoff | Stores token → `/review` |
| `/auth/error` | OAuth failure | None |

## Auth boundary (non-negotiable)

- **Applicants apply without sign-in.** Never gate `/apply` behind OAuth, accounts, or JWT.
- **OAuth is for THP operators/reviewers only** — Google/Meta via Nest `/auth/google`, `/auth/meta`.
- Do not conflate **application** (public intake), **qualification** (operator decision), and
  **diagnostic** (paid engagement). Different objects, different routes, different copy.

## Intake API

| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/intake/applications` | Public | Submit Engagement Readiness form |
| GET | `/intake/applications` | Bearer JWT | List applications (reviewers) |
| GET | `/intake/applications/:id` | Bearer JWT | Application detail |
| PATCH | `/intake/applications/:id` | Bearer JWT | Pipeline tracker updates |

Web submit: server action in `apps/web/src/lib/submit-intake.ts` → `THP_API_URL` (server-side).

**Schema changes:** update Prisma models only — never hand-edit `migrations/**/migration.sql`.
Human runs `pnpm db:migrate`. Destructive migrations require discussion first.
See `07-prisma-database.mdc`.

## Environment variables

| Variable | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `THP_API_URL` | web server | Server-side intake POST (Docker: `http://api:3001`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_THP_API_URL` | web browser | OAuth login URLs, reviewer fetch |
| `DATABASE_URL` | api | Postgres |
| `JWT_SECRET` | api | Operator sessions |
| `AUTH_ALLOWLIST` | api | Optional comma-separated reviewer emails |

Legacy `VITE_THP_API_URL` is dead — use `NEXT_PUBLIC_THP_API_URL`.

## Homepage performance

Cold traffic from YouTube/Instagram must not download the full page at once.

- **Eager:** Hero + canonical letter only (`app/page.tsx`).
- **Lazy:** Below-fold sections via `LazySection` (viewport) + `next/dynamic` (code split) in
  `src/landing/lazy-home-sections.tsx`.
- Do not eagerly import heavy sections (accordion packages, multi-tab grids) into the homepage shell.

## Public funnel destinations

YouTube and campaign CTAs route: **`/work-with-us` → `/apply`**, not `#apply`, not legacy
homepage anchors, not operator sign-in.

